title: Ramu_Day2
tags: 
position: -205,33
---
<<PlayBackgroundMusic Light_3>>
<<SetBGSprite KohliwadaGround>>

The afternoon heat is unforgiving at Koliwada Ground. Despite the sweltering temperature, Raju joins the older boys' game. Ramu comes to watch from the boundary.

The dusty ground shimmers under harsh sun. Raju's decision to test his practice lessons against older players represents a leap in confidence.

<<SetCharacterExpression Sumit Excited>>
Sumit: Come on, Raju! Yesterday your brother said you were special.

<<SetCharacterExpression Sumit Mischievous>>
Sumit: Let's see if you can handle my fastest ball!

<<SetCharacterExpression Raju Confident>>
Raju: Bowl your best, Sumit I'm ready!

<<SetCharacterExpression Raju Pained>>
Raju: Ow! That really hurts...

<<SetCharacterExpression Ramu Worried>>
Ramu: Show me where it hurts.

<<SetCharacterExpression Ramu Furious>>
Ramu: Are you crazy, bowling that hard at an eight-year-old?

<<SetCharacterExpression Ramu Angry>>
Ramu: He could have been seriously injured!

<<SetCharacterExpression Amit Anxious>>
Amit: But bhaiya, he was playing so well!

<<SetCharacterExpression Amit Worried>>
Amit: He hit three boundaries before this.

<<SetCharacterExpression Amit Embarrassed>>
Amit: He said he could handle the fast bowling!

<<SetCharacterExpression Ramu Angry>>
Ramu: I don't care how well he was playing!

<<SetCharacterExpression Ramu Furious>>
Ramu: Look at this bruise!

<<SetCharacterExpression Ramu Angry>>
Ramu: No more for today. You want to break bones over a game?

<<SetCharacterExpression Raju Disappointed>>
Raju: But bhaiya, I was doing really well before this happened.

<<SetCharacterExpression Raju Disappointed>>
Raju: Everyone said I was playing like a much older boy.

<<SetCharacterExpression Raju Confused>>
Raju: Doesn't that matter?

<<SetCharacterExpression Ramu Worried>>
Ramu: That's exactly what scares me.

<<SetCharacterExpression Ramu Serious>>
Ramu: You're too good for your age, too confident.

<<SetCharacterExpression Ramu Anxious>>
Ramu: And confidence can be dangerous when you're small and the game gets rough.

<<SetCharacterExpression Raju Quizzical>>
Raju: Are you angry that I got hurt?

<<SetCharacterExpression Raju Confused>>
Raju: Or angry that I was playing well?

<<SetCharacterExpression Ramu Worried>>
Ramu: I'm angry because... because when you play that well, I start believing.

<<SetCharacterExpression Ramu Serious>>
Ramu: And believing is dangerous for people like us.

<<SetCharacterExpression Ramu Anxious>>
Ramu: What if you get seriously injured chasing this dream?

<<SetCharacterExpression Ramu Serious>>
Ramu: What if you sacrifice everything else and it doesn't work out?

<<SetCharacterExpression Raju Excited>>
Raju: But what if it does work out?

<<SetCharacterExpression Raju Confident>>
Raju: What if yesterday's practice and today's playing mean something?

<<SetCharacterExpression Ramu Serious>>
Ramu: Then you'll need to be more careful. More disciplined.

<<SetCharacterExpression Ramu Serious>>
Ramu: Because if you really have this gift, if you really can make it...

<<SetCharacterExpression Ramu Determined>>
Ramu: Then we can't afford to lose it to some stupid accident on a dusty ground.

<<SetCharacterExpression Raju Excited>>
Raju: So you do think I have talent?

<<SetCharacterExpression Ramu Serious>>
Ramu: Yes. More than I want to admit.

<<SetCharacterExpression Ramu Worried>>
Ramu: More than is safe for me to hope for.

<<SetCharacterExpression Ramu Determined>>
Ramu: That's why we need to be smarter about this.

<<HideAllCharacters>>

As they leave the ground, both understand the day has revealed truths about talent, risk, and the complex calculus of pursuing dreams from their disadvantaged position.

