title: Ramu_Day3
tags: 
position: -151,208
---
<<PlayBackgroundMusic Light_3>>
<<SetBGSprite KohliwadaGround>>
<<HideAllCharacters>>

Evening settles over Kohliwada Ground. Raju seeks out his brother for a different kind of conversation. After two days of intense practice, this quiet moment might be right for difficult questions.

<<HideAllCharacters>>

The ground provides peaceful escape from crowded chaos. Evening shadows lengthen as the harsh heat gives way to gentler warmth.

<<SetCharacterExpression Raju Quizzical>>
Raju: Bhaiya, can I ask you something?

<<SetCharacterExpression Ramu Neutral>>
Ramu: What is it?

<<SetCharacterExpression Raju Quizzical>>
Raju: Why are you always angry when I play cricket?

<<SetCharacterExpression Raju Confused>>
Raju: Even when I do well?

<<SetCharacterExpression Ramu Worried>>
Ramu: ...Because every shot you play makes me nervous.

<<SetCharacterExpression Ramu Serious>>
Ramu: You're too small for such big shots.

<<SetCharacterExpression Ramu Anxious>>
Ramu: And I know how the world treats boys like us who dream too big.

<<SetCharacterExpression Ramu Serious>>
Ramu: And yet... when you hit the ball, when you time it perfectly...

<<SetCharacterExpression Ramu Astonished>>
Ramu: When you send it racing to the boundary, even the older boys stop and stare.

<<SetCharacterExpression Ramu Serious>>
Ramu: Even the men who come to watch start talking about 'that little kid with the natural swing.'

<<SetCharacterExpression Ramu Worried>>
Ramu: That scares me more than your failures ever could.

<<SetCharacterExpression Raju Excited>>
Raju: So you are proud of me?

<<SetCharacterExpression Raju Excited>>
Raju: You do think I can really play?

<<SetCharacterExpression Ramu Serious>>
Ramu: Proud? Hmph. Pride is a luxury we can't afford.

<<SetCharacterExpression Ramu Skeptical>>
Ramu: Pride won't win matches, pride won't put food on the table.

<<SetCharacterExpression Ramu Serious>>
Ramu: Pride won't pay for coaching or equipment or any of the thousand things you'll need.

<<SetCharacterExpression Ramu Proud>>
Ramu: But yes, little brother. When you play - when you really play...

<<SetCharacterExpression Ramu Excited>>
Ramu: Not just swing wildly but actually play with thought and timing...

<<SetCharacterExpression Ramu Smiling>>
Ramu: I see something that makes me believe in things I've taught myself not to believe in.

<<SetCharacterExpression Raju Sad>>
Raju: Then why do you always criticize me?

<<SetCharacterExpression Ramu Serious>>
Ramu: Because hope is dangerous for people like us, Raju.

<<SetCharacterExpression Ramu Worried>>
Ramu: Every time I let myself hope, I remember how easily dreams can be crushed.

<<SetCharacterExpression Ramu Serious>>
Ramu: So I criticize to protect us both. To keep expectations realistic.

<<SetCharacterExpression Raju Quizzical>>
Raju: But doesn't that make it harder to improve?

<<SetCharacterExpression Ramu Smiling>>
Ramu: Maybe. But you seem to be improving anyway.

<<SetCharacterExpression Ramu Proud>>
Ramu: Despite my harsh words, or maybe because of them.

<<HideAllCharacters>>

Their conversation on the ground reveals the emotional complexity behind Ramu's seemingly harsh approach. Both gain deeper understanding of how fear and hope coexist.

