<<PlayBackgroundMusic Light_3>>
<<SetBGSprite KohliwadaGround>>

Three days of consistent practice have created a routine. Today, Raju seeks out his brother at Koliwada Ground to show how the lessons are paying off in real games.

The familiar dust and energy of Koliwada Ground welcome Raju. The public setting creates additional pressure as observers gather to witness his progress.

<<SetCharacterExpression Amit Excited>>
Amit: Bhaiya, your brother's really good!

<<SetCharacterExpression Amit Astonished>>
Amit: Better than kids twice his age. You must be proud!

<<SetCharacterExpression Ramu Proud>>
Ramu: He's just having a lucky day.

<<SetCharacterExpression Ramu Serious>>
Ramu: Tomorrow might be different. Cricket is unpredictable.

<<SetCharacterExpression Raju Excited>>
Raju: Bhaiya! Did you see that six?

<<SetCharacterExpression Raju Overjoyed>>
Raju: It went right over the compound wall!

<<SetCharacterExpression Raju Excited>>
Raju: Just like you taught me - watch the ball, elbow up, follow through!

<<SetCharacterExpression Ramu Skeptical>>
Ramu: ...I saw. But one shot doesn't make a player.

<<SetCharacterExpression Ramu Serious>>
Ramu: Don't get carried away. There's still so much work to do.

<<SetCharacterExpression Raju Disappointed>>
Raju: You never appreciate anything I do.

<<SetCharacterExpression Raju Sad>>
Raju: Even when I use everything you taught me, it's still not enough.

<<SetCharacterExpression Ramu Worried>>
Ramu: It's not that I don't appreciate...

<<SetCharacterExpression Ramu Serious>>
Ramu: It's just that I know how cruel this game can be.

<<SetCharacterExpression Ramu Anxious>>
Ramu: I see your talent growing every day, and that scares me more than I can tell you.

<<SetCharacterExpression Raju Quizzical>>
Raju: Why does my getting better scare you?

<<SetCharacterExpression Raju Confused>>
Raju: Isn't that what you want?

<<SetCharacterExpression Ramu Worried>>
Ramu: Because the better you get, the more people will notice.

<<SetCharacterExpression Ramu Serious>>
Ramu: And when people notice, they expect things.

<<SetCharacterExpression Ramu Anxious>>
Ramu: And when they expect things from poor kids like us...

<<SetCharacterExpression Raju Quizzical>>
Raju: What happens?

<<SetCharacterExpression Ramu Serious>>
Ramu: Sometimes the pressure breaks you.

<<SetCharacterExpression Ramu Worried>>
Ramu: Sometimes the dream becomes so big that reality can't hold it.

<<SetCharacterExpression Ramu Sad>>
Ramu: I've seen it happen, little brother. I've seen boys with talent like yours lose everything.

<<SetCharacterExpression Amit Excited>>
Amit: But bhaiya, what if his dreams aren't impossible?

<<SetCharacterExpression Amit Confident>>
Amit: What if he really can make it?

<<SetCharacterExpression Raju Confident>>
Raju: I can make it happen

<<SetCharacterExpression Ramu Serious>>
Ramu: How should you respond to people recognizing your talent?

<<SetCharacterExpression Ramu Determined>>
Ramu: What approach will you take to prove this is more than just a phase?

<<HideAllCharacters>>

As Ramu poses the crucial question, both brothers stand at a crossroads that will determine whether talent develops into excellence or becomes another cautionary tale.

