<<SetCharacterExpression Raju Serious>>
Raju: Because I see how worried you get, bhaiya.

<<SetCharacterExpression Raju Confident>>
Raju: I'd rather earn your trust gradually than lose it by being reckless.

<<SetCharacterExpression Raju Smiling>>
Raju: Cricket will wait if it means keeping your support.

<<SetCharacterExpression Ramu Astonished>>
Ramu: Your maturity surprises me sometimes.

<<SetCharacterExpression Ramu Excited>>
Ramu: Most kids wouldn't even notice their brother's fears.

<<SetCharacterExpression Ramu Proud>>
Ramu: Let alone want to address them.

<<SetCharacterExpression Raju Serious>>
Raju: Every morning I choose to practice with you because I value what we're building together.

<<SetCharacterExpression Raju Determined>>
Raju: I don't want to rush that or risk damaging it.

<<SetCharacterExpression Ramu Proud>>
Ramu: Your patience and understanding are showing me something important.

<<SetCharacterExpression Ramu Excited>>
Ramu: That maybe your cricket dreams come with the wisdom to pursue them safely.

<<HideAllCharacters>>

As Raju demonstrates emotional maturity by prioritizing his brother's concerns, their relationship evolves from protective oversight to genuine partnership.

<<SetCharacterExpression Ramu Serious>>
Ramu: Then I'll have to learn to hope instead of fear.

